  "body": "From the same Makera Z1 user report (2026-11-11). On their first cut the user cut air, because they hadn't understood where the origin was placed (\"a bit different than what I am used to\"). They fixed it on the **WCS** tab, but: \"it took a while to find out how to actually save the setting, as the 'set origin' button is crammed next to a lot of other options. Couldn't this be next to the close button at the bottom?\"\n\n**What:**\n1. **Make applying the origin obvious.** Put the commit action (Set origin / Apply) in a fixed footer of the WCS page, next to Close, apart from the per-field controls. If edits are pending, make that visible (\"origin not applied\"), so closing never silently discards them.\n2. **Say plainly where the origin is**, in the page header and the setup sheet. For example: \"G54 origin: top of stock, front-left corner (X0 Y0 Z0)\", with a viewport marker that can't be missed. That's the part that made the user cut air.\n3. A short note in the docs or tutorial on how CamCraft places the origin and how to change it.\n\nKeep the change consistent with the WCS page work in #739 (PR #759) and #701 (features with roles). Coordinate with or stack on them where they touch the same page.\n\nEffort: medium (UI).\n\n**Done means:**\n- the commit action sits in a fixed footer beside Close, and pending edits are flagged;\n- the origin's location is stated in words on the page and on the setup sheet;\n- structural ui tests pin both.\n",
